        {"h2_html": "What GoHighLevel <em>does well</em>",
         "body_html": '<p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.85;max-width:64ch">GoHighLevel is a genuinely powerful and flexible platform, and it has earned that reputation. It markets itself as an all-in-one business system that brings a CRM, websites and funnels, email and text messaging, automation, calendars, and reputation tools into a single dashboard, so a business can run much of its sales and marketing in one place instead of stitching five separate tools together. It is deeply customizable, and much of its audience is agencies and marketers, many of whom rebrand it and resell it to their own clients. If you want to be the one in the driver\'s seat and you have the time and the appetite to learn the software, that level of control is a real advantage.</p><p style="color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.85;max-width:64ch;margin-top:1rem">The thing to know going in is that it is software you operate yourself. All of that capability has to be set up, configured, and kept running by someone, and because the platform does so much, there is a learning curve that comes with the power. For an agency or a hands-on marketer, that is exactly the appeal, since they want the keys. For a local owner who is already busy running a business, it can be a lot of platform to learn and manage on top of the actual work.</p>'},
